    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The values of triaxiality γ for protons and those for neutrons are similar in the entire β region (the middle panel of Fig. 1). In the small β region, the system forms an oblate shape with γ ∼ 60◦, while in the large β region around the SD minimum, it forms a triaxial deformation with γ ∼ 10◦. Density distributions of the obtained wave function at the SD minimum [(β, γ) = (0.478, 11.2◦)] are shown in Fig. 2. Because of triaxial deformations around the SD minimum, each wave function contains diﬀerent K components, and two Jπ = 2+ states are obtained after diagonalizing those diﬀerent K components, i.e., K-mixing"
